=== G: score bias, central difference H = 0.01, 200 prior draws, grid weighted by the Volterra
    reference (dt 1.25e-4, t_max 6), full run (96.0 min at 5 cores, 200/200 usable draws) ===

CONTROL G: max |g(analytic)| over v, v_lMTRUE, B, tau, amp_lDTRUE = 0.02077 (must be < 1e-3;
t0 excluded by design, see sbc/malte_m6.R and sbc/score_bias_race.R's own t0 note).
v, v_lMTRUE, B, tau, t0 are all clean (|g(analytic)| <= 0.0019). amp_lDTRUE alone is 0.02077,
21x the floor: the control is INVALID on this parameter.

              v   v_lMTRUE          B         t0        tau amp_lDTRUE
analytic  -0.00185   -0.00006   +0.00006   -0.00001   -0.00010   -0.02077
dt0005    -0.00111   +0.00044   -0.00339   +0.00081   +0.00063   -0.01705
dt005     +0.00013   +0.00043   -0.00139   +0.00195   +0.00103   +0.01626
dt05      +0.01661   +0.01265   -0.06353   -0.00099   +0.02863   -0.38163

Read: for dt 0.0005 and dt 0.005 the flow's own amp_lDTRUE value (-0.017, +0.016) is the same
order as the control's artifact (-0.021), so no real flow bias on this axis can be separated
from the estimator/solver's own noise at H = 0.01, dt = 1.25e-4 -- this screen simply cannot
speak to amp for those two cards. dt 0.05's amp_lDTRUE value (-0.382) is an order of magnitude
past the control's own noise floor, so it stands: consistent with M4 part B's finding that
dt 0.05 is poor on its own terms (KS .018-.16 against the fine reference), reinforced here
independently by score bias.
Not investigated further (would need a smaller H or a finer dt to separate signal from
solver noise on amp specifically, at real additional Volterra cost): flagged for the next
stage, not fixed here.

