=== P: posterior shift ===
NOT RUN TO COMPLETION. Smoke (2 datasets, N = 50 trials, 2 cores, dt 0.0005 card only) ran
4.5 h of wall time (99% CPU on both workers throughout -- genuinely computing, not hung) and
did not finish even one dataset. Cause: each dataset's Laplace fit against the Volterra
reference (dt 1.25e-4, t_max 6) needs an optim() search over the 6-parameter posterior, and
every BFGS/Hessian evaluation costs a fresh Volterra solve (~5 s, benchmarked separately);
convergence to optim's default reltol needs enough evaluations that the wall time is not
minutes but many hours per dataset. This was not budgeted in the registered cost table (which
priced only the D/G-style per-draw cost, not a full posterior optimisation against the
Volterra reference) and is a genuine laptop-time limit, not a bug found in the mechanism
(the same laplace()/importance-sampling code, run against the CHEAP flow accumulator only,
is fast -- it is specifically the analytic/Volterra accumulator inside optim() that is
unaffordable here). Abandoned rather than left running for days or given fabricated numbers.

=== SCREEN lines (registered rule: PASS needs G AND P below their floors with both controls
    valid; G's control here is invalid, which alone reads NOT SEPARATED / a screen failure) ===
SCREEN malte_crdm_aff_log_h2_k12_clip_100k_dt0.0005: FAIL (G control; P not run)
SCREEN malte_crdm_aff_log_h2_k12_clip_100k_dt0.005:  FAIL (G control; P not run)
SCREEN malte_crdm_aff_log_h2_k12_clip_100k_dt0.05:   FAIL (G control; P not run)

Read for the next stage: the FAIL is on the *estimator's* control, not primarily on any card
except dt 0.05 (which fails independently of the control problem, on its own amp_lDTRUE
value and on M4 part B's density numbers). dt 0.0005 and dt 0.005 remain open questions:
their nesting check and their non-amp score-bias numbers are clean, but this screen cannot
currently certify them on amp, and P was not reached at all. Before this screen is trusted
for a real decision, the amp_lDTRUE control needs to be brought under 1e-3 (smaller H,
finer/adaptive dt, or a variance-reduced estimator) and P needs a cheaper route (e.g. a
Laplace-only comparison without the defensive-mixture importance step, or moving straight to
the Gadi SBC cell, which is what the registered rule calls for on an invalid screen anyway).
